    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d333">

                <pb facs="0466" n="370" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg370"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.51/1332</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Assistant Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Dearing</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to President
                        King</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-10-27"><hi rendition="#italic">October 27,
                        1921</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. President</hi>: I have received your
                    letter of October 27, 1921,<anchor n="9" xml:id="d333-f1"/> in which you inform
                    me that the Loan Plan, as redrafted, has your approval and that you are now
                    prepared for the formal signing thereof.</p>
                <p>It is therefore respectfully requested that the members of the Liberian Plenary
                    Commission come to the Department of State tomorrow, Friday, October 28, 1921,
                    at four-thirty p.m. in order that they, in conjunction with the Secretary of
                    State, may sign the Loan Plan and the supplementary Depositary Agreement.</p>
                <p>I remain [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Fred Morris
                    Dearing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
